# workdir
/home/lead
# set-controlling-terminal
false
# notes
- --share-net is passed because bubblewrap runs inside the network namespace that pasta made; it does not share the host's network
- nested user namespaces stay available (owner decision R17): --disable-userns and --assert-userns-disabled are not passed, so code inside can create user namespaces and reach kernel code that is reachable only through them; this is a larger kernel surface than with them disabled
- bind sources (rule G1): no source of a bind lies in or below a host folder the lead can write, because a source is resolved on the host, outside every sandbox, where a symbolic link would be followed; a folder the lead writes is bound whole from an Ataniq-owned parent, and the tree's .git/config, .git/hooks and .git/info are bound from Ataniq's copy of them; a source Ataniq supplies is its real path as the inputs name it and is bound from a descriptor (see the note on descriptors), and a row of the host (/usr, the /etc files) is bound by path, from the real path the holder resolved (Options.HostSources), which bubblewrap resolves by name; this package checks the text of the sources, and the holder checks each source without following links right before the start (mountpoints.CheckBindSources), as a check before the walk that counts
- bind sources by descriptor (rule B1): every bind source Ataniq supplies is bound from a descriptor (--bind-fd, --ro-bind-fd), never by path; the pass-fds step, the last host-side code before bubblewrap, opens the folder each walk starts from without following a symbolic link, walks the path beneath that handle in one openat2 lookup that follows none (RESOLVE_BENEATH, RESOLVE_NO_SYMLINKS), checks on the descriptor it got that the source is the folder or the regular file the row binds, and places that descriptor at the number bubblewrap is given; a source its walk refuses ends the step before bubblewrap starts; whether bubblewrap mounts the object behind the descriptor, and closes the descriptor before the command inside starts, are qualification items that nothing here shows [qualify]
- no seccomp filter: none has been reviewed
- identity: the owner's ids 1000:1001 inside (the fallback mode)
- report channel: the pass-fds step opens the holder's report path write-only as descriptor 3 after pasta, bubblewrap inherits it and the probe inside gets --report-fd 3; the holder takes one accepted probe line as the positive signal and does not wait for end-of-file, because bubblewrap's own processes may keep the descriptor open, and a second line or any further byte after the line is a failure of the start; whether the descriptor reaches the probe inside and which other processes hold it are qualification items that nothing here shows
- bubblewrap keeps and sets PWD under --clearenv: the agent's environment is the allowlist plus PWD=/home/lead, the working folder
- network: pasta arguments of sandboxnet.PastaArgs (outbound NAT, no port forwarding); outbound traffic is not narrowed
- bubblewrap does not make the session (--new-session is never passed): the probe gives the agent its session and controlling terminal, so the launcher does not set a controlling terminal
- optional symlink /lib64 left out: the caller says the host has no such path
- optional symlink /sbin left out: the caller says the host has no such path
- optional read-only bind /etc/ssl left out: the caller says the host has no such path
- optional read-only bind /etc/ca-certificates left out: the caller says the host has no such path
- optional read-only bind /etc/nsswitch.conf left out: the caller says the host has no such path
- optional read-only bind /etc/localtime left out: the caller says the host has no such path
